message.content:
Sure! Below is a simple example of an HTML card that rotates when you hover over it using only CSS (no JavaScript).  
Feel free to copy‑paste this into an `.html` file and open it in your browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* Basic reset */
* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

/* Center the card on the page */
body {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    height: 100vh;
    background: #f0f0f0;
}

/* Card container */
.card {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    perspective: 800px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
    cursor: pointer;             /* Shows pointer on hover */
}

/* Card inner wrapper that will actually rotate */
.card-inner {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    position: relative;
    transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* Smooth rotation */
    transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* Needed for 3D children */
}

/* Front side of the card */
.card-front,
.card-back {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden;       /* Hide backside during rotation */
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    color: white;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    text-align: center;
}

.card-front {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff7e5f, #feb47b); /* Warm gradient */
}

.card-back {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #43cea2, #185a9d); /* Cool gradient */
    transform: rotateY(180deg);   /* Start rotated so it's hidden initially */
}

/* Hover effect: rotate the inner wrapper */
.card:hover .card-inner {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card">
    <div class="card-inner">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="card-front">
            <div>Front Side Content</div>
        </div>
        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="card-back">
            <div>Back Side Content</div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

1. **Perspective** – The `.card` element has `perspective: 800px;`. This gives the 3D effect when we rotate its child.
2. **Transform style** – `.card-inner` uses `transform-style: preserve-3d;` so its children keep their 3D positioning.
3. **Backface visibility** – Both sides have `backface-visibility: hidden;` so the hidden side doesn’t show through.
4. **Hover** – On hovering over `.card`, we rotate `.card-inner` by 180 degrees around the Y‑axis, flipping the card.

You can replace the content inside `.card-front` and `.card-back` with images, text, or anything else you like. Adjust the dimensions, colors, or transition duration to fit your design. Enjoy!
